KG42.register("rules-aa220388e4aabc401bedded4",{"id":"32-wholesale_prosumer_storage::v141-c-R008","paper":"32-wholesale_prosumer_storage","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R008","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local market clearing","process_stage":"clearing","market_meaning":"STEP coordinates the community's supply-demand allocation decisions, including planning community P2P trade and battery utilisation. Scope: STEP coordination of within-community operational allocations in the integrated local and wholesale market design. Supply must be at least the demanded electricity quantity for each house in both stages. The second-stage balance must hold for each renewable-generation and intraday-price scenario. Scope: Household allocations in the community's day-ahead and intraday stages, at every time step. The community allocation model minimizes expected net electricity costs. Grid procurement creates costs, day-ahead grid feed earns compensation, and internal P2P purchases and sales create no community-level cost. Scope: Community-level optimization of local allocations together with wholesale electricity procurement. First-stage supply-demand allocations are based on a single day-ahead production forecast and must anticipate possible second-stage realisations to ensure supply security at lowest cost. Scope: First-stage community supply-demand allocation planning under uncertain second-stage realisations. Resource allocation planned deterministically from the single day-ahead forecast must account for the storage entity's physical restrictions in both stages. Scope: Community resource allocation in model cases permitting residential battery storage. Condition: Battery storage is available.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function clearing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["clearing.local","coordination.local_operator"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R008-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"clearing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM_DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Community resource allocation in model cases permitting residential battery storage. | Community-level optimization of local allocations together with wholesale electricity procurement. | First-stage community supply-demand allocation planning under uncertain second-stage realisations. | Household allocations in the community's day-ahead and intraday stages, at every time step. | STEP coordination of within-community operational allocations in the integrated local and wholesale market design.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g02-e01","v141-b-g02-e03","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e25","v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g03-E04"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"x_P_DA","symbol":"P_DA^(t,h)","meaning":"Day-ahead planned electricity supply of house h in time step t.","kind":"operational","domain":"electricity quantity; sign restriction is not explicitly stated in the quoted clearing equations","unit":null,"indices":["t","h"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e21"]},{"variable_id":"x_Q_DA","symbol":"Q_DA^(t,h)","meaning":"Day-ahead demanded electricity quantity of house h in time step t.","kind":"operational","domain":"electricity quantity; sign restriction is not explicitly stated in the quoted clearing equations","unit":null,"indices":["t","h"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e21"]},{"variable_id":"x_G_DA","symbol":"G_DA^(t,h)","meaning":"Day-ahead planned grid consumption of house h in time step t.","kind":"operational","domain":"electricity quantity","unit":null,"indices":["t","h"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e31"]},{"variable_id":"x_G_ID","symbol":"G_ID^(t,h,s)","meaning":"Intraday grid consumption of house h in time step t and scenario s.","kind":"operational","domain":"electricity quantity","unit":null,"indices":["t","h","s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e32"]},{"variable_id":"x_D_DA","symbol":"D_DA^(t,h)","meaning":"Day-ahead planned battery discharge of house h in time step t.","kind":"operational","domain":"electricity quantity","unit":null,"indices":["t","h"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e27"]},{"variable_id":"x_D_ID","symbol":"D_ID^(t,h,s)","meaning":"Intraday battery discharge of house h in time step t and scenario s.","kind":"operational","domain":"electricity quantity","unit":null,"indices":["t","h","s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e27"]},{"variable_id":"x_I_DA","symbol":"I_DA^(t,h)","meaning":"Day-ahead local P2P electricity purchase of house h in time step t.","kind":"operational","domain":"electricity quantity","unit":null,"indices":["t","h"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e21"]},{"variable_id":"x_I_ID","symbol":"I_ID^(t,h,s)","meaning":"Intraday local P2P electricity purchase of house h in time step t and scenario s.","kind":"operational","domain":"electricity quantity","unit":null,"indices":["t","h","s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e21"]},{"variable_id":"x_C_DA","symbol":"C_DA^(t,h)","meaning":"Day-ahead planned battery charge of house h in time step t.","kind":"operational","domain":"electricity quantity; Eq. (10) gives 0 ≤ C_DA + C_ID ≤ α","unit":null,"indices":["t","h"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e26"]},{"variable_id":"x_C_ID","symbol":"C_ID^(t,h,s)","meaning":"Intraday battery charge of house h in time step t and scenario s.","kind":"operational","domain":"electricity quantity; Eq. (10) gives 0 ≤ C_DA + C_ID ≤ α","unit":null,"indices":["t","h","s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e26"]},{"variable_id":"x_X_DA","symbol":"X_DA^(t,h)","meaning":"Day-ahead local P2P electricity sale of house h in time step t.","kind":"operational","domain":"electricity quantity","unit":null,"indices":["t","h"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e21"]},{"variable_id":"x_X_ID","symbol":"X_ID^(t,h,s)","meaning":"Intraday local P2P electricity sale of house h in time step t and scenario s.","kind":"operational","domain":"electricity quantity","unit":null,"indices":["t","h","s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e21"]},{"variable_id":"x_F_DA","symbol":"F_DA^(t,h)","meaning":"Day-ahead feed of house h into the day-ahead market in time step t.","kind":"operational","domain":"electricity quantity","unit":null,"indices":["t","h"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e31"]},{"variable_id":"x_S","symbol":"S^(t,h,s)","meaning":"Energy storage level in the battery of house h in time step t and scenario s.","kind":"operational","domain":"battery energy storage level, bounded by s_lower and s_upper in Eq. (13)","unit":null,"indices":["t","h","s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e28","v141-b-g02-e29"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"theta_res_forecast","symbol":"res^(t,h)","meaning":"Renewable energy production forecast of house h in time step t.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t","h"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e21"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_res_scenario","symbol":"res_tilde^(t,h,s)","meaning":"Renewable energy production of house h in time step t under scenario s.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t","h","s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e21"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_delta","symbol":"δ^(t,h,s)","meaning":"Renewable production deviation of house h in time step t and scenario s; defined as scenario production minus day-ahead forecast.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"res_tilde^(t,h,s) − res^(t,h)"},"unit":null,"indices":["t","h","s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e21"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_dem","symbol":"dem^(t,h)","meaning":"Inelastic electricity demand of house h in time step t.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t","h"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e21"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_p_G_DA","symbol":"p_G_DA^(t)","meaning":"Dynamic day-ahead grid electricity price in time step t used in Eq. (15); Table 1 prints p_DA^(t).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e31"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_p_F","symbol":"p_F^(t)","meaning":"Dynamic compensation price for electricity fed into the grid in time step t.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e31"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_p_G_ID","symbol":"p_G_ID^(t,s)","meaning":"Uncertain intraday spot price for grid electricity in time step t and scenario s.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t","s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e32"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_pi","symbol":"π_s","meaning":"Probability of occurrence of scenario s; Table 1 prints π_s while Eq. (16) prints π^(s).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e32"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_alpha","symbol":"α","meaning":"Maximum charging rate of the battery.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e26"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_beta","symbol":"β","meaning":"Maximum discharging rate of the battery.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e27"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_eta_c","symbol":"η^c","meaning":"Battery charging efficiency.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e28"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_eta_d","symbol":"η^d","meaning":"Battery discharging efficiency.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e28"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_s_lower","symbol":"s_lower","meaning":"Lower bound of the battery storage level (source prints an underlined s).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e29"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_s_upper","symbol":"s_upper","meaning":"Upper bound of the battery storage level (source prints an overlined s).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e29"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"STEP coordinates the community's supply-demand allocation decisions, including planning community P2P trade and battery utilisation. Scope: STEP coordination of within-community operational allocations in the integrated local and wholesale market design.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Supply must be at least the demanded electricity quantity for each house in both stages. The second-stage balance must hold for each renewable-generation and intraday-price scenario. Scope: Household allocations in the community's day-ahead and intraday stages, at every time step.","expression":"P_DA^(t,h) ≥ Q_DA^(t,h)  ∀t∈T, h∈H;  P_DA^(t,h) + δ^(t,h,s) + D_ID^(t,h,s) + I_ID^(t,h,s) + G_ID^(t,h,s) ≥ Q_DA^(t,h) + C_ID^(t,h,s) + X_ID^(t,h,s)  ∀t∈T, h∈H, s∈S.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_P_DA","x_Q_DA","x_D_ID","x_I_ID","x_G_ID","x_C_ID","x_X_ID"],"parameter_refs":["theta_delta"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e18"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The community allocation model minimizes expected net electricity costs. Grid procurement creates costs, day-ahead grid feed earns compensation, and internal P2P purchases and sales create no community-level cost. Scope: Community-level optimization of local allocations together with wholesale electricity procurement.","expression":"min { ∑_{h∈H}∑_{t∈T} [ p_G_DA^(t) · G_DA^(t,h) − p_F^(t) · F_DA^(t,h) ] + ∑_{t∈T}∑_{h∈H}∑_{s∈S} π_s · p_G_ID^(t,s) · G_ID^(t,h,s) }","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_G_DA","x_F_DA","x_G_ID"],"parameter_refs":["theta_p_G_DA","theta_p_F","theta_p_G_ID","theta_pi"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e01","v141-b-g02-e03","v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g02-e32"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"First-stage supply-demand allocations are based on a single day-ahead production forecast and must anticipate possible second-stage realisations to ensure supply security at lowest cost. Scope: First-stage community supply-demand allocation planning under uncertain second-stage realisations.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g03-E04"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C005","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Resource allocation planned deterministically from the single day-ahead forecast must account for the storage entity's physical restrictions in both stages. Scope: Community resource allocation in model cases permitting residential battery storage. Condition: Battery storage is available.","expression":"0 ≤ C_DA^(t,h) + C_ID^(t,h,s) ≤ α  ∀t∈T, h∈H, s∈S;  0 ≤ D_DA^(t,h) + D_ID^(t,h,s) ≤ β  ∀t∈T, h∈H, s∈S;  S^(t,h,s) = S^(t−1,h,s) + η^c · (C_DA^(t,h) + C_ID^(t,h,s)) − (1/η^d) · (D_DA^(t,h) + D_ID^(t,h,s))  ∀t∈T, h∈H, s∈S;  s_lower ≤ S^(t,h,s) ≤ s_upper  ∀t∈T, h∈H, s∈S;  S^(t0,h,s)=0 for the first time step t0∈T, ∀h∈H, s∈S.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_C_DA","x_C_ID","x_D_DA","x_D_ID","x_S"],"parameter_refs":["theta_alpha","theta_beta","theta_eta_c","theta_eta_d","theta_s_lower","theta_s_upper"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e25","v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g02-e27","v141-b-g02-e28","v141-b-g02-e29"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C006","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The day-ahead planned supply side is the sum of forecast renewable generation, planned grid consumption, planned battery discharge, and local P2P purchase.","expression":"P_DA^(t,h) = res^(t,h) + G_DA^(t,h) + D_DA^(t,h) + I_DA^(t,h)  ∀t∈T, h∈H.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_P_DA","x_G_DA","x_D_DA","x_I_DA"],"parameter_refs":["theta_res_forecast"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e21"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C007","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The day-ahead demanded quantity is the sum of inelastic demand, planned battery charge, local P2P sale, and day-ahead feed.","expression":"Q_DA^(t,h) = dem^(t,h) + C_DA^(t,h) + X_DA^(t,h) + F_DA^(t,h)  ∀t∈T, h∈H.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_Q_DA","x_C_DA","x_X_DA","x_F_DA"],"parameter_refs":["theta_dem"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e21"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C008","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The scenario renewable-production deviation equals scenario renewable production minus the day-ahead forecast.","expression":"δ^(t,h,s) = res_tilde^(t,h,s) − res^(t,h)  ∀t∈T, h∈H, s∈S.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta_delta","theta_res_scenario","theta_res_forecast"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e21"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p02-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"tegration of prosumers in the day-ahead and intraday markets and investigate how rage contributes to","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"To this end, we introduce the Smart elecTricity Exchange Platform (STEP) that represents the interface between the wholesale electricity markets and the prosumer communities, and coordinates the community’s operational supply-demand decisions."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The STEP automatically performs the bidding into the day- ahead market based on the community’s dema","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The STEP automatically performs the bidding into the day-ahead market based on the community’s demand and day-ahead forecasted generation. The STEP is slightly different from aggregator models (see e.g. [33,34]) as it only coordinates the information flows (i.e. a smart box) in the system and does not assume ownership of the electricity. It then acts automatically based on this information, i.e. it bids to or procures electricity from the wholesale market, and plans the P2P trade and battery utilisation in the community. The STEP is not a service providing agent, but rather a computational interface between the wholesale market and the community which makes automatic decisions based on rules specified by the community members. Fig. 2 illustrates the flow of information between the markets and the role of the STEP."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"diagram for the STEP. . • First stage: Balancing for supply-demand operations occurs at - all times ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"First stage: Balancing for supply-demand operations occurs at all times for each house. In this stage, all supply-demand decisions are based on a single day-ahead production forecast subject to an uncertain realisation of supply in the second stage. If more renewable generation than demand is predicted in the community, the houses can choose to jointly bid into the day-ahead market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e01","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"ing the deviations from the day-ahead decisions by adjusting P2P ee- trade, battery usage and procur","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The community comprises a set of heterogeneous prosumers and consumers h ∈ H with different demand and distributed energy resources (solar, wind or batteries). We assume that the residential buildings are located such that the generation patterns among them are correlated but diversified. All buildings are connected to the main grid and interconnected by a local grid. This framework is modelled using a two-stage stochastic linear program. The model minimises the community’s expected costs of procuring electricity from the wholesale markets."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e03","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"market. In this paper, the market design allows P2P trade among ec- prosumers and consumers in a com","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"For the integration of communities into the existing electricity markets, we propose a bidirectional connection from the local market to the main electricity markets. This entails a virtual connection allowing for trade, and physical connections of individual buildings with the main power grid. To jointly plan loads and charging in the local market as well as bidding and scheduling decisions in the day-ahead market, we introduce a Smart elecTricity Exchange Platform (STEP). This platform aims at minimising the expected costs for the community’s local market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"g ) g q y q y e 3 each house h ∈ H in each time step t ∈ T . Eq. (1) represents the t market-clearin","equation_id":"Eq. (1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"A market-clearing equation ensures the security of supply for each house in each time step. Hence, the supply has to be (in both stages) greater or equal to the demanded electricity quantity of each house h ∈ H in each time step t ∈ T. Eq. (1) represents the market-clearing equation for the first stage in which all day-ahead market variables are denoted with the subscript DA. P_{DA}^{(t,h)} ≥ Q_{DA}^{(t,h)} \\qquad (1). All first stage decisions hold true for all t ∈ T and h ∈ H, while all second stage constraints are additionally valid for all s ∈ S."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e18","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p06-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"y p of house h in time step t f house h in time step t and scenario s f house h from peer p in time ","equation_id":"Eqs. (2)-(3), (5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Eq. (5) summarises the market-clearing equation for the second stage which holds true for each house h ∈ H and each time step t ∈ T depending on the scenarios s ∈ S for renewables and intraday prices. DA supply + DG deviations + ID battery discharge + ID P2P purchase + ID grid: P_{DA}^{(t,h)} + δ^{(t,h,s)} + D_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} + I_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} + G_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} ≥ Q_{DA}^{(t,h)} + C_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} + X_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} \\qquad (5). DA demand + ID battery charge + ID P2P sale."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e25","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p07-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"3.2.3. Storage restrictions The privately owned storages are limited by their physical char- ma acte","equation_id":"Eqs. (10)-(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The privately owned storages are limited by their physical characteristics. The storage entities link the two stages of the proposed model as they combine the day-ahead and intraday decisions. Based on the single day-ahead forecast, the model plans the allocation of resources deterministically, albeit taking into consideration the physical restriction of the storage entity for both stages."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e30","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p07-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"y y p grid at dynamic real-time prices and compensations are paid when 4.2 electricity is fed into t","equation_id":"Eqs. (14)-(15)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The objective of the model is to minimise costs of electricity for the community. Costs arise when electricity is procured from the grid at dynamic real-time prices and compensations are paid when electricity is fed into the day-ahead market. The two-stage model incorporates two market stages that add stage-specific components to the overall objective function. That is, the objective function is split into the day-ahead (O_{DA}) and intraday market (O_{ID}) objectives, see Eq. (14). min {O_{DA} + O_{ID}} \\qquad (14)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e31","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p07-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"y y p grid at dynamic real-time prices and compensations are paid when 4.2 electricity is fed into t","equation_id":"Eqs. (14)-(15)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The day-ahead objective, Eq. (15), comprises the day-ahead planned grid consumption G_{DA}^{(t,h)} at the dynamic price p_{G\\_DA}^{(t)} and the day-ahead feed-in F_{DA}^{(t,h)} at a dynamic compensation p_{F}^{(t)}. Costs for P2P trade do not arise at community level as the P2P purchase of one peer is at the same time the sale of another. O_{DA} = \\sum_{h,t} [p_{G\\_DA}^{(t)} · G_{DA}^{(t,h)} − p_{F}^{(t)} · F_{DA}^{(t,h)}] \\qquad (15)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E04","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p11-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":11,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"ado et al. / Energy & Buildings 184 (2019) 163–176 strong grid consumption or infeed. The STEP marke","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-11.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The consideration of uncertainty plays an important role in a system relying on renewable energy sources. By the proposed two-stage stochastic programming approach, the model’s decisions reflect the incorporation of uncertainty in renewable production and intraday prices: The decisions made for day-ahead market participation in the first stage is based on a single forecast of supply, subject to the second stage constraints. The second stage, in turn, considers a set of possible discrete scenarios of realisation. The supply-demand balance has to be satisfied in each of the scenarios. Hence, the decisions made in the first stage need to anticipate the possible level of realisation in the second stage to ensure security of supply at lowest costs."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"gy g y XDA(t,h ) day-ahead P2P electricity sale of house XID(t,h,s ) intraday P2P electricity sale o","equation_id":"Eqs. (2)-(3), (5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"DG + DA grid + DA battery discharge + DA P2P purchase: P_{DA}^{(t,h)} = res^{(t,h)} + G_{DA}^{(t,h)} + D_{DA}^{(t,h)} + I_{DA}^{(t,h)} \\qquad (2)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e16","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"gy g y XDA(t,h ) day-ahead P2P electricity sale of house XID(t,h,s ) intraday P2P electricity sale o","equation_id":"Eqs. (2)-(3), (5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Demand + DA battery charge + DA P2P sale + DA feed: Q_{DA}^{(t,h)} = dem^{(t,h)} + C_{DA}^{(t,h)} + X_{DA}^{(t,h)} + F_{DA}^{(t,h)} \\qquad (3)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e17","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"intraday market at reserve market prices is an option. These prices are also uncertain. Eq. (5) summ","equation_id":"Eqs. (4)-(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The deviations δ^{(t,h,s)} enter the second stage balancing constraint resulting from the difference of renewable scenarios res^{(t,h,s)} and day-ahead forecast res^{(t,h)}: δ^{(t,h,s)} = \\widetilde{res}^{(t,h,s)} - res^{(t,h)} \\qquad (4)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e21","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p06-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"J.M. Zepter, A. Lüth and P. Crespo del Granado et Table 1 Designated sets, parameters and variables ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Table 1 Designated sets, parameters and variables of the mathematical model. Sets: t ∈ T hours t in time horizon T; h, p ∈ H houses h and peers p in community H; s ∈ S scenarios s in set of scenarios S. Scalars: \\psi^{P2P} efficiency factor for conversion and transmission of DG sources to P2P sale; \\underline{s}/\\overline{s} upper/lower bounds of storage level in battery; α/β maximum charging/discharging rate of battery; η^{c}/η^{d} battery charging/discharging efficiency. Parameters: dem^{(t,h)} demand of house h in time step t; res^{(t,h)} renewable energy production of house h in time step t; \\widetilde{res}^{(t,h,s)} renewable energy production of house h in time step t and scenario s; δ^{(t,h,s)} deviations in production of house h in time step t and scenario s; π_{s} probability of occurrence of renewable scenario s; p_{DA}^{(t)} price of electricity from the grid in the day-ahead market in time step t; p_{ID}^{(t,s)} price of electricity from the grid in the intraday market in time step t and scenario s; p_{F}^{(t)} price of electricity fed into the grid in time step t; p_{P2P}^{(t)} price of electricity in the local market in time step t. Variables: C_{DA}^{(t,h)} day-ahead charge of battery of house h in time step t; C_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} intraday charge of battery of house h in time step t and scenario s; D_{DA}^{(t,h)} day-ahead discharge of battery of house h in time step t; D_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} intraday discharge of battery of house h in time step t and scenario s; F_{DA}^{(t,h)} day-ahead feed of house h in time step t; G_{DA}^{(t,h)} day-ahead grid consumption of house h in time step t; G_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} intraday grid consumption of house h in time step t and scenario s; I_{DA}^{(t,h)} day-ahead P2P electricity purchase of house h in time step t; I_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} intraday P2P electricity purchase of house h in time step t and scenario s; I_{p,ID}^{(t,h←p,s)} intraday P2P electricity purchase of house h from peer p in time step t and scenario s; P^{(t,h)} day-ahead planned electricity supply of house h in time step t; Q^{(t,h)} day-ahead demanded electricity quantity of house h in time step t; S^{(t,h,s)} energy storage level in battery of house h in time step t and scenario s; X_{DA}^{(t,h)} day-ahead P2P electricity sale of house h in time step t; X_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} intraday P2P electricity sale of house h in time step t and scenario s; X_{p,ID}^{(t,h→p,s)} intraday P2P electricity sale of house h from peer p in time step t and scenario s."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e26","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p07-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"3.2.3. Storage restrictions The privately owned storages are limited by their physical char- ma acte","equation_id":"Eqs. (10)-(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The summed charges in each stage C_{DA}^{(t,h)} and C_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} are for one time step bounded by the charge rate α, Eq. (10). 0 ≤ C_{DA}^{(t,h)} + C_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} ≤ α \\qquad (10)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e27","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p07-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"3.2.3. Storage restrictions The privately owned storages are limited by their physical char- ma acte","equation_id":"Eqs. (10)-(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The sum of discharges D_{DA}^{(t,h)} and D_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} are limited by the discharge rate β, specified in Eq. (11). 0 ≤ D_{DA}^{(t,h)} + D_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} ≤ β \\qquad (11)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e28","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p07-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"is calculated from the intertemporal change of energy compared to the prior storage level in time st","equation_id":"Eqs. (12)-(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The final realisation of charge and discharge comprises the sum of the decisions in the two stages. The storage level S^{(t,h,s)} is calculated from the intertemporal change of energy compared to the prior storage level in time step t−1, S^{(t−1,h,s)}. The level changes when the battery is charged by C_{DA}^{(t,h)}/C_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} or discharged by D_{DA}^{(t,h)}/D_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} in a time step t ∈ T in either stage. Charging and discharging are subject to the efficiency rates η^{c} and η^{d}, as detailed in Eq. (12). S^{(t,h,s)} = S^{(t−1,h,s)} + η^{c} · (C_{DA}^{(t,h)} + C_{ID}^{(t,h,s)}) − (1/η^{d}) · (D_{DA}^{(t,h)} + D_{ID}^{(t,h,s)}) \\qquad (12)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e29","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p07-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"is calculated from the intertemporal change of energy compared to the prior storage level in time st","equation_id":"Eqs. (12)-(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The amount of energy S^{(t,h,s)} stored in the battery has to comply the lower and upper battery bounds \\underline{s} and \\overline{s}, as specified in Eq. (13). The storage level in the first time step of the optimised day starts at zero in each scenario s ∈ S. \\underline{s} ≤ S^{(t,h,s)} ≤ \\overline{s} \\qquad (13)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e32","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"ado et al. / Energy & Buildings 184 (2019) 163–176 . In the intraday market, costs arise when electr","equation_id":"Eq. (16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In the intraday market, costs arise when electricity is procured from the wholesale intraday market G_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} at an uncertain intraday spot price p_{G\\_ID}^{(t,s)}. The intraday market’s expected objective value is obtained from the sum over the scenarios while taking into account their respective probabilities. O_{ID} = \\sum_{t,h,s} π^{(s)} [p_{G\\_ID}^{(t,s)} · G_{ID}^{(t,h,s)}] \\qquad (16)"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","quote":"To this end, we introduce the Smart elecTricity Exchange Platform (STEP) that represents the interface between the wholesale electricity markets and the prosumer communities, and coordinates the community’s operational supply-demand decisions."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e06","quote":"It then acts automatically based on this information, i.e. it bids to or procures electricity from the wholesale market, and plans the P2P trade and battery utilisation in the community."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","quote":"A market-clearing equation ensures the security of supply for each house in each time step. Hence, the supply has to be (in both stages) greater or equal to the demanded electricity quantity of each house h ∈ H in each time step t ∈ T."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e18","quote":"Eq. (5) summarises the market-clearing equation for the second stage which holds true for each house h ∈ H and each time step t ∈ T depending on the scenarios s ∈ S for renewables and intraday prices."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e01","quote":"The model minimises the community’s expected costs of procuring electricity from the wholesale markets."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e03","quote":"This platform aims at minimising the expected costs for the community’s local market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e30","quote":"The objective of the model is to minimise costs of electricity for the community. Costs arise when electricity is procured from the grid at dynamic real-time prices and compensations are paid when electricity is fed into the day-ahead market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e31","quote":"Costs for P2P trade do not arise at community level as the P2P purchase of one peer is at the same time the sale of another."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e07","quote":"In this stage, all supply-demand decisions are based on a single day-ahead production forecast subject to an uncertain realisation of supply in the second stage."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E04","quote":"The supply-demand balance has to be satisfied in each of the scenarios. Hence, the decisions made in the first stage need to anticipate the possible level of realisation in the second stage to ensure security of supply at lowest costs."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e25","quote":"Based on the single day-ahead forecast, the model plans the allocation of resources deterministically, albeit taking into consideration the physical restriction of the storage entity for both stages."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"37edce6b796f987b70cb28ecb5dc6d3c59716fd89ee4406f1f918b6f6046b4d2","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The frozen clearing rule has source-supported mathematical content in the supplied B evidence: first-stage and scenario-wise second-stage supply-demand inequalities, the day-ahead and intraday objective terms, and battery physical restrictions. C001 and C004 lack a standalone source formula and remain procedural/not_formalized. This formalization is provisional because B evidence is unreviewed and not independently source-audited; notation inconsistencies remain noted in revision_requests.","bindings":[{"object_id":"x_P_DA","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Operational clearing variable in the local supply-demand allocation."},{"object_id":"x_Q_DA","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Operational clearing variable in the local supply-demand allocation."},{"object_id":"x_G_DA","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Operational clearing variable for day-ahead grid consumption."},{"object_id":"x_G_ID","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Operational clearing variable for intraday grid consumption."},{"object_id":"x_D_DA","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Operational clearing variable for day-ahead battery discharge."},{"object_id":"x_D_ID","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Operational clearing variable for intraday battery discharge."},{"object_id":"x_I_DA","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Operational clearing variable for day-ahead P2P purchase."},{"object_id":"x_I_ID","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Operational clearing variable for intraday P2P purchase."},{"object_id":"x_C_DA","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Operational clearing variable for day-ahead battery charge."},{"object_id":"x_C_ID","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Operational clearing variable for intraday battery charge."},{"object_id":"x_X_DA","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Operational clearing variable for day-ahead P2P sale."},{"object_id":"x_X_ID","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Operational clearing variable for intraday P2P sale."},{"object_id":"x_F_DA","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Operational clearing variable for day-ahead feed."},{"object_id":"x_S","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Operational storage-state variable constrained inside local clearing."},{"object_id":"theta_res_forecast","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Forecast parameter used by clearing supply definitions."},{"object_id":"theta_res_scenario","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Scenario parameter used by second-stage clearing."},{"object_id":"theta_delta","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Scenario-deviation parameter used in second-stage clearing."},{"object_id":"theta_dem","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Demand parameter used by local clearing."},{"object_id":"theta_p_G_DA","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Day-ahead price parameter in the clearing objective."},{"object_id":"theta_p_F","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Feed-in compensation parameter in the clearing objective."},{"object_id":"theta_p_G_ID","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Intraday price parameter in the expected clearing objective."},{"object_id":"theta_pi","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Scenario-probability parameter in the expected clearing objective."},{"object_id":"theta_alpha","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Battery charge-rate parameter in clearing storage restrictions."},{"object_id":"theta_beta","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Battery discharge-rate parameter in clearing storage restrictions."},{"object_id":"theta_eta_c","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Battery charging-efficiency parameter in clearing storage restrictions."},{"object_id":"theta_eta_d","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Battery discharging-efficiency parameter in clearing storage restrictions."},{"object_id":"theta_s_lower","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Battery lower-bound parameter in clearing storage restrictions."},{"object_id":"theta_s_upper","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Battery upper-bound parameter in clearing storage restrictions."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","clearing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R008-E001"],"rationale":"The frozen edge links STEP/local coordination to local clearing; it represents the procedural coordination constraint."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R008-C002","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The supply-demand inequalities are constraints on the local clearing function."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R008-C003","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The objective expression belongs to the local clearing optimization."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R008-C005","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Storage physical restrictions are modeled inside local clearing."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R008-C006","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The day-ahead supply definition supports the local clearing balance."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R008-C007","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The day-ahead demand definition supports the local clearing balance."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R008-C008","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The scenario deviation definition supports the second-stage clearing balance."}],"revision_requests":["No graph revision is requested, but B evidence remains unreviewed and not independently source-audited; this formalization is provisional.","Notation inconsistency for later canonical mapping: Table 1 defines P^(t,h), Q^(t,h), and p_DA^(t), while Eq. (1) uses P_DA/Q_DA and Eq. (15) uses p_G_DA^(t). C.1 should confirm whether these are intended aliases if canonical symbol linking is required.","Eq. (16) prints π^(s) whereas Table 1 prints π_s; C.1 should confirm the intended probability symbol.","The source states a 7.6% P2P transmission and conversion loss but does not in the quoted clearing evidence give the exact ψ^P2P multiplier; no numeric ψ value is asserted here."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
